-- 206_supergun_se_request_encoding.surql -- how the SIM asks for a sound, how a request becomes a wave, and a
-- live defect that was silently dropping every sound effect after 64 ticks.
-- 2026-09-07. supergun-steam-re-expert (encoding, ring, bank table) + the wasm lane (cue->wave, decoder, gate).
-- Supersedes the "timing/perf object INFERRED" label on FRAME-READSET.md:67.
USE NS re DB kb;

UPSERT source:supergun_sound_20260907 SET kind='disasm', strength='code',
  ref='GhidraMCP decompiles of FUN_14006B5D0 (ring append), FUN_14006B6E0 (dispatcher), FUN_1408454B0 (post SE), FUN_140609990/1406095F0/140609570/140609510/140609760/140609D60 (game-side posters), FUN_1401FF8B0 (sSound::setSeEntryNum), FUN_1402926C0 (SRQR lookup), FUN_14006BD40 (bank path build), FUN_140613CD0; strings sSound::NativeSystemXAudio2::WinProperty, sSound::UpdateThread, Snddrv; bank name table 0x140A4FED0; pan table 0x14097D5A0; plus parsing of the owner own game_5s.arc and two live battle anchors.',
  note='Answers SHELL-DESIGN-REVIEW.md:152 "audio: not yet". Cites finding:frame_writes_audio_command_ring_outside_blk (seed 187) which already held the ring.';

UPSERT finding:supergun_se_request_encoding SET status='confirmed', confidence='high', date='2026-09-07',
  contribution_candidate=true,
  title='The sim posts sounds into a 16-byte command ring at *(0x142EBC010); the id packs channel/cue/bank/side',
  statement='The simulation neither calls sSound nor writes a DC-style byte queue. It appends 16-byte records {op, arg1, arg2, arg3} to a 64-entry ring at SND+0x346AC (SND = *(0x142EBC010)), with the count at SND+0x34AAC capped at 0x40 by FUN_14006B5D0. Op 8 plays a sound effect, 9 stops, 10 sets volume, 11 sets pan; op 2 is the MUSIC level and is posted EVERY tick by FUN_140609D60 inside FUN_140608A00 (⚠ this line said 'master volume' when first written and was wrong: FUN_14006B6E0 case 2 sets a volume on the STREAM handle at SND+0x34260, and FUN_140609D60 ramps a float toward a target before posting it, so it is the music fade). Op 0 plays a stream cue+0xA8 on that same handle, op 5 stops it, op 1 plays with a fade. Ops 6 and 7 are the MIXER: op 6 writes bus i (i<8) at SND+0x3466C, op 7 restores its default. The eight buses are named by FUN_1401EE3A0 -- Total, Se, Bgm, Env, Voice, System, Event, LFE -- and their live floats are a contiguous block at SND+0x33278 (getters FUN_1401F79C0/FUN_1401F7200/FUN_1401F5D60 read +0x33278/+0x3327C/+0x33280, which fixes the index order by measurement). A ring volume byte is scaled by DAT_1408E33E4 = 1/127 exactly, so it is a linear gain. arg2/arg3 are signed bytes in the low byte, -1 meaning leave default. The 32-bit id in arg1 packs, high to low: channel 0..7, cue index, bank index, and a low byte of 0xA8 neutral / 0xA9-0xAA per side. Bank indexes the 128-entry name table at 0x140A4FED0 (pl00..pl3a, 0x3C/0x3D comn, 0x3E syuk, 0x3F staf). The dispatcher forms a voice as channel*0x100 + (id & 0xFF), and a new sound on a voice replaces the one there. Pan is a bucket from the 16-entry table at 0x14097D5A0, 50..78 with 64 centre.',
  consequence='A shell that replaces sSound reads this ring directly and never calls FUN_14006B690/FUN_14006B6E0, which would enter sSound through bank handles a stubbed host has not built. The request path touches only blk, ctx and this object, reaching zero file/D3D/socket/HID/audio imports, and it sits inside FUN_140608A00 which is UPSTREAM of the host flush -- so --no-flush does not suppress it. This is NOT the config+0x520 trap.',
  caveat='Every SE post is wrapped in `G+0x43 != 0 || G+0x14 != 0x40`. FUN_14060B440 is the only writer of G+0x43 and sets it 1 at mode entry, so the gate passes in normal play; measured 1 on two live anchors.';

UPSERT finding:supergun_sound_ring_overflow_drops_everything SET status='confirmed', confidence='high', date='2026-09-07',
  contribution_candidate=true,
  title='Nothing zeroed the sound command count, so after 64 ticks every request was silently discarded',
  statement='FUN_14006B5D0 appends only `if (count < 0x40)`. The shipped host zeroes the count at the top of its frame (0x140039DFA) and drains at the bottom (0x14003A4A1, a tail jump after the frame call). No SUPERGUN shell did either, and FUN_140609D60 posts one op-2 every single tick, so the ring reached 64 entries in 64 ticks and every later request -- including every sound effect -- was dropped with no error and no log.',
  consequence='Any audio work must zero the count per presented frame first, or sound plays for about one second and stops. PROVEN FREE: with the count zeroed before every tick, the 1000-tick select->load->battle gate stays byte-identical to a native runner that does not zero it (1000/1000 blk plus gs, exe_dat, exe_rt, ggpo, exe_str, ctx under the narrow mask, dcram including the tile buffer).',
  caveat='Rollback duplicates: depth-N re-runs append N times and can overflow, discarding the CORRECTING tick commands. Zero the count at the start of a catch-up burst, not only per frame.';

UPSERT finding:supergun_cue_to_wave_mapping SET status='confirmed', confidence='high', date='2026-09-07',
  contribution_candidate=true,
  title='cue -> wave is SRQR record +74, and the waves are MS-ADPCM in game_5s.arc',
  statement='game_5s.arc is the same ARC v7 container as game_50.arc but multi-entry: 1604 entries of 80 bytes (name[64], u32 extHash, u32 compSize, u32 decompSize, u32 offset), each payload individually zlib. It holds 1479 waves (ext 0x724DF879), 62 sound banks (SBKR, 0x15D782FB), 62 request tables (SRQR, 0x1BCC4966) and one stream table (STQR, 0x167DBBFF). In an SRQR the count is a u32 at +8 and records are 0x90 bytes from offset 0, carrying a u16 cue index at +72 that counts 0,1,2..., a u8 wave slot at +74 and a u8 volume at +75. The record base and field offsets were located BY FINDING THE COUNTER rather than by trusting a struct guess. The matching SBKR holds one full archive path per slot. Waves are RIFF/WAVE format tag 2, MS-ADPCM, mono, about 48 kHz, 70-byte blocks of 128 samples, coefficients carried in the file.',
  consequence='A browser can play the game own sound effects from the user own archive with no baking: resolve bank+cue to a path, inflate, decode. An MS-ADPCM decoder written for this was gated byte-exact against ffmpeg on four waves spanning 34,048 to 403,840 samples, 0 differing samples. Validated against a real session: pl17 cue 10 and pl13 cue 10 resolve to that character wave 10, and comn 145/51/69 to real waves.',
  caveat='⚠ The MS-ADPCM predictor divides TOWARD ZERO; using an arithmetic shift floors, and because the result feeds the next sample that one bit compounds -- measured differences up to 86 starting at the third sample, with sample COUNTS still matching, so nothing structural flags it. ⚠ Some cues resolve to a wave named "blank": deliberate silence, not a miss (pl17 cues 42/43 fire constantly and are blanks).';

RELATE finding:supergun_se_request_encoding->cites->source:supergun_sound_20260907 SET id='e206_enc_src';
RELATE finding:supergun_sound_ring_overflow_drops_everything->cites->source:supergun_sound_20260907 SET id='e206_ring_src';
RELATE finding:supergun_cue_to_wave_mapping->cites->source:supergun_sound_20260907 SET id='e206_cue_src';
RELATE finding:supergun_se_request_encoding->cites->finding:frame_writes_audio_command_ring_outside_blk SET id='e206_enc_prior';
RELATE finding:supergun_sound_ring_overflow_drops_everything->cites->finding:supergun_se_request_encoding SET id='e206_ring_enc';
RELATE finding:supergun_cue_to_wave_mapping->cites->finding:supergun_se_request_encoding SET id='e206_cue_enc';

UPSERT finding:supergun_bgm_is_ogg_vorbis_by_cue SET status='confirmed', confidence='high', date='2026-09-07',
  contribution_candidate=true,
  title='Music is requested by cue on a separate stream handle, and the tracks are plain Ogg Vorbis on disk',
  statement='The sim asks for music through the SAME 16-byte command ring as sound effects but on a DIFFERENT handle: op 0 plays stream cue+0xA8 on SND+0x34260 (FUN_14006CB70), while every effect op indexes the bank array at SND+0x34268. Op 5 stops, op 1 plays with a fade, op 2 sets the level. The cue map is the single STQR entry in game_5s.arc (`sound\bgm\mvc2\snd_mvc2_bgm_org_all`, ext 0x167DBBFF): u32 name count at +8 and u32 CUE count at +12 (23 names, 30 cues -- cues share tracks), with the cue table at 0x3E8, stride 152, the cue own index at +0 and the NAME INDEX at +92. The record layout was found by searching for the field that counts 0,1,2..., not by trusting a struct guess. A name is an archive path like `sound\bgm\mvc2\wav\selc` and the audio is the matching `.sngw` beside the install arc folder -- which is PLAIN OGG VORBIS, OggS magic, vorbis identification header, 48 kHz, no obfuscation.',
  consequence='A browser needs no decoder for music at all: fetch the .sngw and hand it to decodeAudioData. Gated: 30/30 cues resolve to an Ogg file that exists on the owner install (bgm_gate.mjs). This is why music was silent in a shell that drained the ring correctly -- it watched the effect handle only.',
  caveat='⚠ Vorbis is decoded by Chrome and Firefox but NOT Safari. ⚠ The STQR entry TOC dsize carries flag bits (0x40000000), so it is not a plain size -- inflate on the compressed size instead of comparing the two.';

RELATE finding:supergun_bgm_is_ogg_vorbis_by_cue->cites->source:supergun_sound_20260907 SET id='e206_bgm_src';
RELATE finding:supergun_bgm_is_ogg_vorbis_by_cue->cites->finding:supergun_se_request_encoding SET id='e206_bgm_enc';
